ive in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ecd7d48-e192-56ba-a9eb-6c4280135677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234667}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ecd7d48-e192-56ba-a9eb-6c4280135677" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234667} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1bfa42a-8d4e-593c-aa9b-c50e784fddb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235263}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "615b21ea-17f4-5ce5-8433-316c3df76ca0" :question/math-academy-id "q-167787" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x)\n$$\n\nThe order of this differential equation is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ." :question/worked-solution "We have the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}},$ which has order $4.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ac80f9-d1a9-57b5-8a75-ee4e690886f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250849} {:answer/id #uuid "254a46ec-eea5-5a9e-b90d-ccb407bc95b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250874} {:answer/id #uuid "625479f9-bef7-5c1a-937a-158ca732f7fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251352} {:answer/id #uuid "c2b7f046-3e73-5ab4-abac-a3903f00d5ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252273} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ca56e0-ad02-5c3f-97f9-85ad61671b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22ac80f9-d1a9-57b5-8a75-ee4e690886f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250849} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fc95c7a-43dc-5a46-8131-164063c49bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253003}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81cebd09-5186-5bea-8883-e39dc896a0be" :question/math-academy-id "q-118779" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{6}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{6}}+3x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}={x}^{8}?$" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{6}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{6}},$ which has order $6.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uui