m "Which of the following are second-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}+{y}^{′}={x}^{2}-x$\n- **II.** ${y}^{‴}-y=x-{y}^{″}$\n- **III.** ${x}^{3}{y}^{′}+x=y$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of second-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{″}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″}.$\n\n- Equation II is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation III is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{′},$ so this is a first-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53060f3c-37ba-5269-99e6-437127908eb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358467} {:answer/id #uuid "779e8577-9f6e-5fa7-924b-e37a99f1b28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358783} {:answer/id #uuid "8704391c-698c-5b53-8da1-2de5b7777a0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358934} {:answer/id #uuid "aab69c40-d839-5b4b-94d1-7d9e857ba71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359221} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d51d2e-5951-5e07-ab5d-d620a48d77f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aab69c40-d839-5b4b-94d1-7d9e857ba71c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359221} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9cba9eb-cca7-50bc-8d85-f1b4fa7b959a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e716837-33b2-54de-96d4-f505ade9217f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96662" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+5{y}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+3{y}^{5}=0?$" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}},$ which has order $3.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360692 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7c8253-2398-5844-ab87-9f569178c088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358387} {:answer/id #uuid "604bb718-8188-5706-9d5e-bc5e825254c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358594} {:answer/id #uuid "64729ba5-db61-5904-a7f3-3348bf688c82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358631} {:answer/id #uuid "95c21078-c3b5-5a29-a41b-fa3dd5c92b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359063} {:answer/id #uuid "9903b498-b87b-528c-9348-0e7f32f90a53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95c21078-c3b5-5a29-a41b-fa3dd5c92b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359063} :answer-field/id #uuid "4becacdb-3199-5e03-8693-24305826113a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360114}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "21e5af7d-c901-55dc-94b7-2ce8f4a4e5f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-96663" :question/problem "What is the order of the ordinary differential equation $y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}}-4{x}^{2}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=2x?$" :question/worked-solution "The order of an ordinary differential equation (ODE) is the order of the highest derivative in the equation.\n\nThe highest derivative in the given ODE is $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{4}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{4}},$ which has order $4.$\n\nTherefore, the order of the ODE is $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360693 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30abb0c4-1bff-50f9-9fca-c00eba3cf9ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422285} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe184a0-615a-5d44-a917-af918964b500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebe184a0-615a-5d44-a917-af918964b500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422286} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ba99938-250e-5ae5-bf0d-5fb8ffd0e043" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422423} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18a407fa-f792-5416-9af8-1c23d1ca46fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422287} {:answer/id #uuid "d6eee552-87f0-587e-9972-7d671e2c86b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6eee552-87f0-587e-9972-7d671e2c86b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422288} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07ca297-62a7-5e03-8fea-27d8baa6b5a5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422424} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed3c95ff-45e3-5a8f-97c1-8b53553ad9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422289} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae2557d-e9db-57cc-b828-db6340b0d291" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed3c95ff-45e3-5a8f-97c1-8b53553ad9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422289} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb037b0-ed04-5067-99cf-fa5cc12a74f1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422425}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1054102-ae5b-5062-8507-4d26889215d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96672" :question/problem "Which of the following are second-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${y}^{″}{x}^{3}-2y{y}^{′}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$\n- **II.** $3{y}^{″}{y}^{′}-2y=2{y}^{′}$\n- **III.** $4{y}^{‴}x-7{x}^{2}{y}^{′}=y{e}^{x}$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of second-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{″}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation I is a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″}.$\n\n- Equation II is also a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{″}.$\n\n- Equation III is not a second-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{‴},$ so this is a third-order differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation"}]}
